---
import EvidenceFrame from '../../components/EvidenceFrame.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;

const decisions = [
  {
    title: 'Policy is part of the request',
    copy: 'Memory Only stops when no scoped memory matches. Memory + Model may continue with Ollama, but the response is explicitly labeled as model knowledge rather than retrieved evidence.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Retrieval stays inspectable',
    copy: 'The API returns expanded search queries, counts, selected sources, snippets, metadata, and the query-analysis trace instead of hiding the retrieval path behind one answer string.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Scope has two enforcement points',
    copy: 'Namespace and domain constraints can become Chroma metadata filters; term and tag rules are checked again against retrieved documents before selection.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Reasoning and records are separate concerns',
    copy: 'The reasoning endpoint can remain stateless, while the investigate endpoint wraps the same pipeline and writes a durable SQLite artifact with its brief and report.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Inquiry Engine case study — Chad Hamilton"
  description="A verified engineering case study of Inquiry Engine: a local-first research interface connected to FastAPI, Chroma retrieval, Ollama reasoning, and SQLite investigation records."
>
  <article class="case-study inquiry-case">
    <header class="case-hero section-pad">
      <div class="shell">
        <a class="back-link" href={`${base}#work`}><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Selected work</a>
        <div class="case-hero__grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Case study / Inquiry Engine</p>
            <h1>A local reasoning system that shows how an answer was assembled.</h1>
          </div>
          <div class="case-hero__summary">
            <p>Inquiry is used to ask questions across a personal knowledge collection, choose the kind of reasoning wanted, constrain which memory may participate, inspect the resulting evidence, and retain useful work as an investigation.</p>
            <div class="tag-row">
              <span>Research interface</span>
              <span>Retrieval + local AI</span>
              <span>Persistent investigations</span>
            </div>
            <a class="button button--primary case-live-link" href="https://github.com/icyNatural/inquiry-backend-omen" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View public backend <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="case-visual shell">
      <EvidenceFrame
        src={`${base}images/projects/inquiry/desktop-interface.png`}
        alt="Connected Inquiry Observatory desktop result showing the pollinator-garden answer, routing trace, three retrieved records, and source evidence"
        label="Inquiry Observatory / Connected desktop"
        caption="A real local inquiry after the React frontend called FastAPI, retrieved three isolated Chroma records, reasoned with Ollama, and saved the investigation to SQLite."
        width={1440}
        height={1000}
        eager={true}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="case-facts section-pad-sm">
      <div class="shell case-facts__grid">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Frontend</span><strong>React 19 · TanStack Start · TypeScript</strong></div>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">API</span><strong>Python · FastAPI · Pydantic</strong></div>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Retrieval</span><strong>Chroma · all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings</strong></div>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Reasoning + records</span><strong>Ollama · SQLite</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-rule">
      <div class="shell narrative-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Purpose / 01</p><h2>A cockpit for deliberate questions, not a generic chat box.</h2></div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>The interface makes consequential choices visible before a request begins. Six implemented modes—Recall, Synthesis, Raw, Framework, Grounding, and Mapping—change the response structure. A knowledge policy decides whether the engine must stay inside retrieved memory or may use the local model when memory is absent.</p>
          <p>Advanced scope controls restrict namespaces, domains, tags, and terms. After processing, the interface can present the answer beside routing details and source evidence. Investigation records have their own API for listing, editing, versioning, deleting, and retaining parent references.</p>
          <div class="callout"><strong>Verified boundary:</strong> this run used only an isolated Chroma collection with three synthetic demonstration notes. External retrieval was disabled, and no private local corpus participated. Browser workspace, continuity, and graph surfaces also contain local-interface capabilities beyond the backend’s current investigation schema.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-dark">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading--light">
          <p class="eyebrow">Active architecture / 02</p>
          <h2>One request crosses explicit retrieval, reasoning, and persistence boundaries.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="architecture-flow" aria-label="Inquiry Engine active request architecture">
          <div class="architecture-node"><span>01</span><strong>Observatory UI</strong><small>Question · mode · scope · policy</small></div>
          <div class="architecture-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="architecture-node"><span>02</span><strong>FastAPI</strong><small>Pydantic request validation</small></div>
          <div class="architecture-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="architecture-node"><span>03</span><strong>Retrieval</strong><small>Query expansion · Chroma · scope · diversify · rerank</small></div>
          <div class="architecture-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="architecture-node"><span>04</span><strong>Ollama</strong><small>Source interpretation · mode prompt · response</small></div>
          <div class="architecture-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="architecture-node"><span>05</span><strong>Investigation</strong><small>Answer + provenance written to SQLite</small></div>
        </div>
        <p class="architecture-note">Active orchestration lives in <code>legacy_inquiry_engine.investigate()</code> despite its filename. The separate class-based cognition implementation and files under <code>app/legacy/</code> are not on this FastAPI request path.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-rule">
      <div class="shell runtime-example">
        <div class="runtime-example__intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Verified run / 03</p>
          <h2>A real interface request with retrieval and persistence.</h2>
          <p>This end-to-end run connected the current React frontend to an unchanged isolated copy of the local FastAPI backend on September 20, 2026. It used three synthetic garden notes in a dedicated Chroma store, called the locally installed <code>gemma3:4b</code> model through Ollama, and created one SQLite investigation. It did not use private notes.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="runtime-steps">
          <li><span>Question</span><strong>Recall the watering rule for the public demonstration pollinator garden.</strong></li>
          <li><span>Mode + policy</span><strong>Recall · unrestricted scope · Memory + Model</strong></li>
          <li><span>Retrieved context</span><strong>Four deterministic search queries; 3 retrieved and 3 selected chunks</strong></li>
          <li><span>Model processing</span><strong>Ollama reranked and interpreted the retrieved notes; general model knowledge was not used as evidence</strong></li>
          <li><span>Response</span><strong>Water deeply Tuesday and Saturday unless the previous seven days brought at least 25 millimeters of rain; check soil moisture first</strong></li>
          <li><span>Saved investigation</span><strong>Version 1 retained the question, policy, scope, search queries, nine pipeline stages, answer, three sources, and timestamp</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <EvidenceFrame
          src={`${base}images/projects/inquiry/saved-investigation.png`}
          alt="Inquiry Observatory Investigation Records view showing the saved pollinator-garden inquiry and its SQLite-backed raw record"
          label="Inquiry Observatory / Persisted record"
          caption="The same interface loaded the one saved investigation from FastAPI and displayed its question, model, retrieval counts, pipeline stages, answer, and source records."
          width={1440}
          height={1000}
          tone="light"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad system-section">
      <div class="shell system-section__grid">
        <div class="system-section__copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Interface detail / 04</p>
          <h2>The connected result remains inspectable on a narrow screen.</h2>
          <p>The current interface keeps the answer, routing trace, retrieval counts, and evidence readable on a narrow screen. The connected mobile capture shows the same real investigation rather than a configured placeholder state.</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Six backend-executable cognition modes</li>
            <li>Memory Only and Memory + Model policies</li>
            <li>Namespace, domain, tag, and term constraints</li>
            <li>Typed client with an honest engine-offline state</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="fine-print">This is the connected result from the same isolated interface run shown above. External retrieval was disabled and the demo store contained no private material.</p>
        </div>
        <EvidenceFrame
          src={`${base}images/projects/inquiry/mobile-interface.png`}
          alt="Connected mobile Inquiry Observatory showing the watering-rule answer, routing details, and retrieved context from the isolated demo store"
          label="Inquiry Observatory / Connected mobile"
          caption="The real answer and retrieval trace remain inspectable at 390×844."
          width={390}
          height={844}
          tone="light"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-rule">
      <div class="shell outcome-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Engineering decisions / 05</p><h2>Guardrails are expressed in data and control flow.</h2></div>
        <div class="decision-list">
          {decisions.map((decision) => (
            <article><h3>{decision.title}</h3><p>{decision.copy}</p></article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad section-dark">
      <div class="shell narrative-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Implementation status / 06</p><h2>What is active, and what remains historical.</h2></div>
        <div class="prose implementation-status">
          <p><strong>Active:</strong> FastAPI routes, the module-level inquiry orchestrator, centralized Chroma and embedding access, scope filtering, retrieval diversification, soft Ollama reranking, source interpretation, mode-specific prompting, two knowledge policies, and SQLite investigation CRUD.</p>
          <p><strong>Not on the active request path:</strong> the older server and cognition files under <code>app/legacy/</code>, duplicated class-based cognition methods, the dormant module-level history list, and planned question-strategy symbols such as automatic follow-up generation.</p>
          <p><strong>Runtime:</strong> Docker was not required by the active local startup path. The verified stack used the documented Vite command, native Uvicorn/FastAPI, native Ollama, an isolated Chroma directory, and an isolated SQLite database.</p>
          <p><strong>Validation:</strong> the current local backend test suite passed 22 tests with one Starlette deprecation warning. The connected frontend production build also completed successfully, and browser verification reported no console errors or failed requests while loading the saved record.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="case-next" aria-label="Project navigation">
      <div class="shell case-next__inner"><span>Next project</span><a href={`${base}projects/energy-engine/`}>Energy Engine <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Layout>